      "anchor": "lifts-finite-common-polarisation-scale",
      "title": "A positive rational polarisation scale with all the required valuations",
      "hypotheses": "Fix a rational prime p, a unit c of the restricted finite adeles away from p, and a rational s>0 giving the local duality test at p.",
      "statement": "There is a unique s₁>0 with vₚ(s₁)=vₚ(s) and v_q(s₁)=v_q(c_q) at all other finite primes. Then ε=s₁/c and its inverse are integral away from p, and multiplication by s₁ or by s gives the same p-local integrality test.",
